# ZooKeeper Health Check — Deployment Runbook

**Environment:** Apigee OPDK Preprod  
**Author:** Rakesh  
**Date:** 2026-03-22  
**Status:** Deployed & Verified ✅

---

## Overview

Automated ZooKeeper health monitoring script deployed across all 3 ZK nodes in the Apigee OPDK preprod cluster. The script runs every 5 minutes via cron, performs 10 health checks per node, and logs results to `/var/log/zk_health.log` with 14-day logrotate retention.

---

## Cluster Details

| Node IP | Hostname | Role |
|---|---|---|
| ZK-NODE-1-IP | ZK-NODE-1-HOSTNAME | Follower |
| ZK-NODE-2-IP | ZK-NODE-2-HOSTNAME | Follower |
| ZK-NODE-3-IP | ZK-NODE-3-HOSTNAME | Leader |

- ZooKeeper Port: `2181`
- Quorum requirement: 2 out of 3 nodes
- OneAgent (Dynatrace): running on all nodes

---

## What the Script Checks

| # | Check | Method | Threshold |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Node availability | `echo ruok \| nc` → expects `imok` | Must return imok |
| 2 | Node role | `echo srvr \| nc` → grep `Mode:` | leader or follower |
| 3 | Average latency | `mntr` → `zk_avg_latency` | Warn if > 500ms |
| 4 | Outstanding requests | `mntr` → `zk_outstanding_requests` | Warn if > 10 |
| 5 | Alive connections | `mntr` → `zk_num_alive_connections` | Logged |
| 6 | Pending syncs | `mntr` → `zk_pending_syncs` | Logged |
| 7 | Ephemeral nodes | `mntr` → `zk_ephemerals_count` | Logged |
| 8 | Watch count | `mntr` → `zk_watch_count` | Logged |
| 9 | Quorum validation | Sum of reachable nodes | CRITICAL if < 2/3 |
| 10 | Leader count | Count of leader-mode nodes | CRITICAL if != 1 |

